From b6b47dc8dc0b656c808e84ec1cabd6df5f3a2573 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:14:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(import): resolve OBJ face references against vertex
 records

The OBJ reader merged duplicate vertex positions and then resolved face
references against the shortened unique list. A legal file that repeats
a vertex record was refused ("vertex reference '5' out of range"), and a
reference in range of the short list could name the wrong position.

The reader now keeps one entry per `v` record that maps to its unique
position. Positive and negative references resolve against the records
read so far. Out-of-range, zero and past-the-start references are still
refused by line.

Fixes #3298

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
